Individual Case Safety Report (ICSR)

1. Introduction

An Individual Case Safety Report (ICSR) is a structured report containing information about one or more suspected adverse reactions experienced by an individual patient following exposure to a medicinal product.

ICSRs are essential in pharmacovigilance for collecting, assessing, documenting, and reporting suspected adverse drug reactions (ADRs) to support medicine safety monitoring.

2. Objectives

- To understand the structure and purpose of an ICSR.
- To identify and document a suspected adverse drug reaction.
- To assess case validity and completeness.
- To perform causality assessment using the Naranjo algorithm.
- To classify the reaction based on severity and seriousness.
- To evaluate expectedness using reference safety information.
- To understand the principles of regulatory safety reporting.

